  "rationale": "The workflow already caches Gradle dependencies through `actions/setup-java@v4` with `cache: gradle`, which is the equivalent dependency-cache optimization described by pattern P-LIT-GHA-CACHE. That pattern lists \"An equivalent cache already exists\" as a contraindication, so adding a separate `actions/cache` step for `~/.gradle/caches` would be redundant rather than a minimal, coverage-preserving improvement. No other pattern applies cleanly: the workflow has a single job with no matrix, so fail-fast, stale-run cancellation, and build-prioritization optimizations are not relevant, and no test-selection or timeout changes are supported by the repository context.",
  "evidence_ids": ["pattern:P-LIT-GHA-CACHE"]
